      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mooers%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Riverside Cemetery, located at Route 11 and Mills Street, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2018.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        20,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mooersny.com/historian/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1932 border inspection station was built to accommodate growing traffic between Mooers, NY, and Quebec, Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mooersny.com/historian/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Construction of the Great Northern railroad began in 1848 and finished in 1850, making it the town’s first railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mooersny.com/historian/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mooers Campground on Campground Road and the former Mooers High School serve as living reminders of the town’s deep‑rooted history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mooersny.com/historian/"
    },
    {
